{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121293","id":4039744546,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7wyZwi","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121293","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121293.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121293.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121293","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121293/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121293/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121293/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1e49e61970ca0f775e8179e2980bf1092d526eba","number":121293,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Decouple FALLOFF & SHADOW from ATTENUATION","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15040\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis PR decouples LIGHT_FALLOFF and LIGHT_SHADOW built-ins from ATTENUATION built-in in light() function, allowing using them individually. This makes it possible to write more flexible light() functions with less performance impact than doing workarounds that achieve the same visual result.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n- Expose new LIGHT_FALLOFF and LIGHT_SHADOW built-ins inside light() function.\r\n- Strip-out ATTENUATION, LIGHT_FALLOFF, LIGHT_SHADOW if one is unused and if it's safe to do so.\r\n- If LIGHT_FALLOFF and LIGHT_SHADOW are both used - ATTENUATION is stripped-out and later derived from falloff & shadow.\r\n- Dont strip-out ATTENUATION if no light() is defined, because it's used in default light() function.\r\n\r\nThat way it passes minimum 0, maximum 2 built-ins, and 1 if only one of them is used.\r\n\r\nStripping-out is there to optimize VGPR register usage and keep it the same as it was when only ATTENUATION is used, as passing 2 new built-ins unconditionally is overkill.\r\n\r\nHere's the pseudocode of its logic:\r\n\r\n```\r\nif LIGHT_FALLOFF is used:\r\n\tpass only LIGHT_FALLOFF\r\n\r\nif LIGHT_SHADOW is used:\r\n\tpass only LIGHT_SHADOW\r\n\r\nif custom light() is NOT defined:\r\n\tpass ATTENUATION because default light() function uses it.\r\n\r\nif custom light() is defined:\r\n\tif both LIGHT_FALLOFF and LIGHT_SHADOW are used:\r\n\t\tderive ATTENUATION from falloff & shadow\r\n\telse:\r\n\t\tpass ATTENUATION\r\n```\r\n\r\nNamings that i've came up with:\r\n\r\n- ATTENUATION_DISTANCE & ATTENUATION_SHADOW\r\n- LIGHT_FALLOFF & SHADOW\r\n- FALLOFF & SHADOW\r\n- LIGHT_FALLOFF & LIGHT_SHADOW (current, reflecting [this proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15040))","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-07-12T17:37:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T15:59:20Z","closed_at":"2026-09-09T15:59:03Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d87461e061db095e67e87ea97aa17b671ab4573e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":null,"ref":"master","repo":null,"sha":"1e49e61970ca0f775e8179e2980bf1092d526eba","user":null},"base":{"label":"godotengine:master","ref":"master","repo":{"id":15634981,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxNTYzNDk4MQ==","name":"godot","full_name":"godotengine/godot","owner":{"login":"godotengine","id":6318500,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjYzMTg1MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6318500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/godotengine/orgs","repos